ink":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T22:57:17-08:00","id":1500431,"title":"","content":"This inspired me to do a write-up of my own game notes on this: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-groove-stolen</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-23T01:52:09-08:00","id":1500435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500405-tips-for-rewriting-the-monastery-scene-in-blood-fire?p=1500423#post1500423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would go for more radical changes. They might mess up with canon but you would have a more intense and interesting experience. <br /> A suggestion: instead of focusing on just the Paths, there could be the Sabbat equivalent of a Council of Trent, where the different ideologies present in the sect gather in an attempt to define their doctrine regarding issues such as Caine and Lilith (setting up the banning of the banning of Bahari), the nature of vampirism, the position regarding the Antediluvians, the Gehenna, and so on. You could have people representing the Lasombra catholics, the Metamorphosists, the Black Hand and many others.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a great idea. I could imagine visiting luminaries who'd contribute to the debates, tortured prisoners who'd share their knowledge in exchange for mercy, experimentation with the means of breaking blood bonds and binding the new Sabbat together, the formulation of early ritae, debates on how the sect should be governed and managed, and so on. <br /> <br /> It would be a mixture of idealists, pragmatists and opportunists, all gathered together to build something new and enduring to protect themselves -- and then maybe each other.<br /> <br /> My own solution to this, prior to this thread, was to have the Black Monastery become a refuge for the remaining paragons of the old Roads -- those who'd agreed to serve the Sabbat in exchange for survival, at any rate.<br /> <br /> RAW, the retcon was that the Anarchs diablerised most of the elders who were Road paragons, thus resulting in the loss of most of that knowledge. The Anarchs mainly targeted their own elders so they could break the chains of their own bondage, however, which means some of those paragons were probably slain by fellow followers on their own Road. <br /> <br /> Those neonates and ancillae might have some imperfect knowledge of the Roads, and some of them would likely be involved in the formulation of the new Paths (and help explain why they were simplified or bastardised).<br /> <br /> There might also be some elder paragons who saw an opportunity to fill the leadership roles their dead peers once filled, and took it, as well as those who genuinely sided with the Anarchs' cause.<br /> <br /> Add in that the Camarilla is shifting to low-key Humanity, making the Roads unwelcome, and that the Inquisition is a religious movement that would see organised Roads as blasphemy, it might make sense for the surviving members of the Roads to seek shelter with the Sabbat. <br /> <br /> Some of those might have heard of a well-guarded sanctuary they could reach at the Black Monastery.<br /> <br /> If you combine the two ideas, you could have a very compelling chapter. There are refugees from the Roads present, plus the founding idealists/extremists of the sect who want to forge a new society for all Cainites. <br /> <br /> They have a shared goal: to make the Sabbat safer/more stable for themselves and each other, to create new ways to fight the Beast, and to lay out the doctrine that will unite them as the Sword of Caine. <br /> <br /> They could witness not just the emerging Paths, but also the ritae the elders are practising. Some of that might look like strange sorcery to the characters, so that Intisar's work on the Path of Revelations seems less conspicuous as a result.<br /> <br /> You might even see the beginnings of the Sabbat clergy at this point, with some residents calling themselves cardinals and archbishops, with a table of 12 paladins charged with protecting them.<br /> <br /> There could also be hints of the future factions that will emerge in the sect -- maybe Dastur Anosh is there, or one of the Black Hand Seraphim; maybe the predecessors of the Sabbat Inquisition are also there; maybe there are already ideological splits akin to the Moderates, Ulta Conservatives and Loyalists.<br /> <br /> The different factions would influence each other and butt heads in a variety of ways. Your PCs would be left to wonder which elders are in it for the cause, who's in it for survival or opportunism, and whether any of these creatures are actually loyal to the Sabbat they're creating.<br /> <br /> After the vampires at the Monastery finish their business, the paladins probably go their own separate ways and train up the first templars; the archbishops head off to their former domains and try to claim those cities for the Sabbat; the acolytes of the new Paths would become the first priests; and so on.<br /> <br /> If done right, the players (and their characters) should see and understand the Sabbat viewpoint a little better, and perhaps even be tempted to join. <br /> <br /> Either way, they will leave with some very useful context about vampire politics that may stand them in good stead in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-23-2022, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-23T03:46:05-08:00","id":1500444,"title":"","content":"Another thing I would do it'd be setting it earlier than 1666, if it fits your Chronicle. It always seemed to me that 166 years was too long before the Sabbat decided to do that. As an analogy, the Council of Trent happened 100 years earlier","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}